# The registered codable-options1 plan (toolchain a0.0.45) rewrites every
# retired wire marker as a `#Codable` option, in a source and in a Markdown
# file's prose and fence: `#Encode` and `#Decode` as `only:`, both directions
# and either beside `#Codable` as plain `#Codable`, a field's `#Skip` and
# `#[Flatten]`, `#DenyUnknownFields`, `#Discriminant(k)` (in a string too,
# escapes kept, and after a string's `\n` escape), `#Untagged` and
# `#PublishedSchema` stacked on its own line above `#Codable`, beside the
# markers it leaves (`Debug`, `Rename(.Camel)`). `#CodableAsBase` goes, with
# its line when it stood alone. `#!Encode`, whose spelling depends on a
# hand-written decoder, and a keyless `#Discriminant` are reported and left,
# and `C#` and `#Encoded` stay. A second run finds nothing left to rewrite.
